// One stop on the companion's route: a world-file entity of kind "companion_stop". The route is
// scripted, not found by an AI: she walks from stop to stop, in `order`, when the player has
// come near enough.
//
// Properties set on the entity in the world editor:
// - `order` (number): the stop's place in the route, 0 first.
// - `wait_seconds` (number): the least time she waits here before walking on.
// - `boost` (number, optional, 1 = yes): she crouches here and doesn't walk on until the player
//   has jumped off her back (see BoostSystem).
// - `speed` (number, optional): metres per second to the next stop; 4.5 when missing.
// - `swing` (number, optional, 1 = yes): she crosses to the next stop by swinging the Anchor whose
//   start post is beside this stop, ahead of the player, instead of walking the whole way. She
//   walks on from the far post to the next stop, so that stop sits on the far side.
// - `near` (number, optional): metres the player must be within before she walks on from here. Left
//   out, she walks on when the player is within her usual lead range, or already ahead of her (she
//   then hurries). Set, she waits for exactly that and never hurries on ahead: a gap crossing by
//   her light uses a small one, a swing a large one so the player sees her go first.
CompanionStop :: class {
public:
    position: lantern:::math:::Vec3;
    order: i32;
    waitSeconds: f32;
    isBoost: bool;
    speedToNext: f32;
    isSwing: bool;
    hasMeetDistance: bool;
    meetDistance: f32;

    CompanionStop~: (entity: i64) : position(lantern:::world:::Position(entity)),
        order(i32(lantern:::world:::NumberProperty(entity, "order"))),
        waitSeconds(lantern:::world:::NumberProperty(entity, "wait_seconds")),
        isBoost(lantern:::world:::HasProperty(entity, "boost") && lantern:::world:::NumberProperty(entity, "boost") > 0.5f),
        speedToNext(lantern:::world:::HasProperty(entity, "speed") ? lantern:::world:::NumberProperty(entity, "speed") : 4.5f),
        isSwing(lantern:::world:::HasProperty(entity, "swing") && lantern:::world:::NumberProperty(entity, "swing") > 0.5f),
        hasMeetDistance(lantern:::world:::HasProperty(entity, "near")),
        meetDistance(lantern:::world:::HasProperty(entity, "near") ? lantern:::world:::NumberProperty(entity, "near") : 0.0f) { }
}
